.TH MDHTML 2
.SH NAME
mdhtml \- Markdown to HTML
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "mdhtml.m";
mdhtml := load Mdhtml Mdhtml->PATH;

init:   fn();
html:   fn(text: string): string;
escape: fn(s: string): string;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Html
returns the Markdown document
.I text
as HTML, by the rules of Markdown.pl (John Gruber's, which werc
formats its pages with), for a page a browser shows.
.I Init
must be called first.
.PP
Blocks are paragraphs; headings, by
.B #
to
.B ######
or a line of
.B =
or
.B -
under their text; rules
.RB ( --- ,
.BR "* * *" );
block quotes, nested and with lazy lines; lists by
.BR * ,
.BR + ,
.B -
or a number and
.BR . ,
nested by indentation, tight (items' text bare) or loose (in
paragraphs) as blank lines put them, an ordered list keeping a first
number other than 1; code indented four spaces, or between fences of
.B ```
or
.B ~~~
(the first word after the opening fence its
.BR language- class);
and raw HTML, a line at the left margin opening a block-level element,
taken as it is to the next blank line (and
.BR <pre> ,
.BR <script> ,
.B <style>
and
.B <textarea>
to their end tag, a comment to its end).
Reference definitions,
\fB[\fIid\fB]: \fIurl\fR and, if it has one, \fB"\fItitle\fB"\fR
on a line of their own, are taken out wherever they are.
.PP
Inline: code spans of any number of backticks; emphasis and strong
emphasis by
.B *
and
.B _
(an
.B _
inside a word is a letter);
.B ~~
for deleted text; links and images, inline
\fB[\fItext\fB](\fIurl\fB "\fItitle\fB")\fR
or by reference
.RB ( [\fItext\fP][\fIid\fP] ,
.BR [\fItext\fP][] ,
.BR [\fItext\fP] );
autolinks
.RB ( <http://...> ,
.BR <mailto:...> ,
.BR <name@host> );
raw inline HTML and entities passed through; backslash escapes; a
line ending in two blanks a hard break.
Other
.BR & ,
.B <
and
.B >
are escaped.
What is written as HTML is passed through unchanged: a document is
trusted as its author's, as it is in werc.
Do not give
.I html
text from someone who must not write HTML into the page.
.PP
.I Escape
returns
.I s
with \fB&\fP, \fB<\fP, \fB>\fP and \fB"\fP
as entities, for text or an attribute's value.
.PP
.IR Rlayout 's
.B parsemd
.RB ( module/rlayout.m )
parses Markdown to draw it, in Xenith's Render, and drops what a page
needs (images, raw HTML, list nesting, references); this is the one
that writes it out as HTML.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/lib/mdhtml.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR wercfs (4)
.SH BUGS
It is Markdown.pl's dialect, not CommonMark: tables are paragraphs,
headings have no ids, and emphasis is matched by a simpler rule than
CommonMark's.
